  "hindi": "तुम सबमें जो हैं, उनमें सबसे श्रेष्ठ के लिए हम उत्तम स्तुति आगे अर्पित करते हैं, जैसे हवि लाते समय प्रज्वलित होते अग्नि के लिए। अजर, बुढ़ापा लाने वाले, सींचे हुए, पुरातन काल से तरुण इन्द्र को हम सहायता के लिए बुलाते हैं।",
  "english": "We offer forth a good praise to the most excellent of you who are, as to Agni when he is being kindled and the oblation is borne. We call for help Indra, unaging, causing to age, sprinkled, young from of old.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The verb for pra (and the offering of the praise) is not stated; 'we offer' is supplied from the sense, havāmahe being the only finite verb. satām taken as gen. pl. of the participle 'being' ('of you who are'); 'of the good ones' is possible. jarayantam is the causative participle ('making age'); object not stated. ukṣita 'sprinkled' (or 'grown strong'; the sense in this context is not certain).",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
