  "hindi": "महान् इन्द्र, जिसके बिना कुछ भी नहीं है, जिसमें सब वीर कार्य एकत्र हैं, वह पेट में सोम को, शरीर में महान् बल को, हाथ में वज्र को और सिर में संकल्प को धारण करता है।",
  "english": "Great Indra, without whom there is nothing at all, in whom all heroic deeds are gathered together: in the belly he bears Soma, in the body great might, in the hand the vajra, in the head resolve.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "kiṃ cana īm ṛte has no verb; 'there is' is supplied. yasmād indrād bṛhataḥ is taken as a relative clause governing ṛte (ablative). The t of 'tsaṃbhṛtā' belongs to asmin (asmin + saṃbhṛtā), a sandhi insertion; adhi taken with saṃbhṛtā ('gathered in'). tanvī3 (loc. of tanū with a protraction mark 3) and bharati taken as serving all four locatives; mahaḥ read as an adjective of sahaḥ. kratu rendered 'resolve' throughout (could be 'power, intelligence').",
