  "hindi": "तेरा बल दोनों पृथ्वियों से घेरा नहीं जा सकता, और हे इन्द्र, तेरा रथ न समुद्रों से, न पर्वतों से। जब तू तेज चलने वालों के साथ बहुत से योजनों के पार उड़ता है, तब कोई भी तेरे वज्र तक नहीं पहुँचता।",
  "english": "Your power is not to be encompassed by the two earths, nor your chariot, Indra, by the seas or the mountains. No one at all reaches your vajra when you fly with the swift ones across many stretches.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "te before indriyam is printed 'ta' (RV sandhi te + i -> ta i). kṣoṇī in the dual is taken as 'the two earths' (probably Heaven and Earth, but the verse does not say so). paribhve taken as a dative infinitive used predicatively ('is not to be encompassed'). 'the swift ones' (āśubhiḥ) are not named in the verse (horses suggested by context). puru is printed short (purū would be expected as n. pl.); kept as given, no flag since the length mark is a metrical matter.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.016.3a",
   "002.016.3b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "न क्षो॒णीभ्यां॑ परि॒भ्वे॑ त इन्द्रि॒यं न स॑मु॒द्रैः पर्व॑तैरिन्द्र ते॒ रथ॑:",
   "न ते॒ वज्र॒मन्व॑श्नोति॒ कश्च॒न यदा॒शुभि॒: पत॑सि॒ योज॑ना पु॒रु"
  ],
